    <metadataclass count="1" name="General">
      <metadata id="1536" net="1">
        <attribute name="Name" id="1537" net="1">
          <![CDATA[Beaver dam building and wetland creation]]>
          <graphics count="0"/>
        </attribute>
        <attribute name="Description" id="1538" net="1">
          <![CDATA[Beavers as ecosystem engineers: a pair scouting a stream, felling trees and building a dam, the pond rising while the dam holds (inhibitor cap), floods that breach the dam and drain the pond (reset arc) with repairs only while the colony is present (read arc), a lodge once the water is deep, ducks, frogs and marsh plants colonising in parallel, a winter food cache that must be full before freeze-up, kits, years of use until the aspen is exhausted, abandonment, a draining pond becoming beaver meadow, and aspen regrowth that invites a new colony.]]>
          <graphics count="0"/>
        </attribute>
        <graphics count="0"/>
      </metadata>
    </metadataclass>
